drvdiff -- run the REAL pico_driver.c on the desktop and capture exactly what it
would send to the panel.

visdiff (tests/picodiff) covers pic DECODE only. The driver half -- flush_region,
pico_blit_indexed, draw_line, draw_filled_rect, grab/restore, bake_static_region,
the BACK restore -- had NO offline coverage, and that is where the 16-bit LCD
attempt died: one writer converted, the rest still emitting the old format, only
visible as a sheared picture on hardware.

pico_driver.c's hardware surface is small (13 functions), so drvstub.c stands in
for it and captures hw_send_spi -- the bytes that actually reach the panel --
plus every define_region_spi header, because correct pixels sent to the wrong
window are still a wrong picture.

Packed vs unpacked is a COMPILE-TIME choice, so this builds TWICE and diffs the
captures rather than linking two renamed copies.

  cd tests/drvdiff
  LIBS=$(find ../../build -name '*.a' | tr '\n' ' ')
  for cfg in "" "-DPICO_PACK_VISUAL=1"; do
    out=$([ -z "$cfg" ] && echo unpacked || echo packed)
    gcc -fgnu89-inline -w -include stdint.h -DHAVE_CONFIG_H=1 -DX_DISPLAY_MISSING=1 \
        -DHAVE_PICO=1 -DPICO_DITHER_D16=1 $cfg \
        -I. -I../../src/include -I../../build -I/usr/include/SDL2 -D_REENTRANT \
        -o drvdiff_$out drvdiff_main.c ../../src/gfx/drivers/pico_driver.c drvstub.c \
        -Wl,--start-group $LIBS -Wl,--end-group -lSDL2 -lm -lz -lpthread -ldl
  done
  ./drvdiff_unpacked cap_unpacked.bin && ./drvdiff_packed cap_packed.bin
  cmp cap_unpacked.bin cap_packed.bin      # must be identical

  PPM=1 ./drvdiff_unpacked cap.bin         # also dumps cap.bin.ppm to LOOK at

Baseline with nothing converted: 192,020 bytes captured (20-byte region header +
320*200*3 RGB), 16 distinct colours, packed == unpacked.

TWO TRAPS, both of which produced a silently BLANK or flat frame and no error:
 - gfx_color_t.mask must be set (GFX_MASK_VISUAL) or every draw is a no-op.
 - a cel needs colors/colors_nr; a NULL palette collapses every index to one
   colour. colors_nr 256 selects the identity path, as backgrounds use.
